From 530c1c548e89dfe65e21376401c66d4e44571cb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:59:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Digimon ids: DigimonId parameters and partner-type locals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step 3 of docs/mods/ids.md (§ 10), the u8 Digimon parameters.

- loadNPCModel, unloadDigimonModel and scriptSetDigimon take a DigimonId.
  They had one definition with u8 parameters (overworld.c) and a second,
  int32_t prototype in script_interp.c; there is now one prototype in
  model.h, so LOAD/SET/UNLOAD_DIGIMON16 hand the whole type over.
- Locals that held the partner's type in a u8 before comparing it with a
  u8 list (cup fair/eligible lists, tournament registration, baby types,
  the tournament pool) and the speaker's type in getSpeakerName keep the
  whole type, so a type above 255 no longer matches its low byte.

The u8 lists themselves (cups, BABY_IDS, RegisteredDigimon) are content
and save data; they move with the content build and save v2.

---
 include/dw/model.h       |  4 ++++
 src/dget/dget.c          |  5 +++--
 src/main/overworld.c     |  9 +++------
 src/main/script_common.c |  2 +-
 src/main/script_interp.c |  4 +---
 src/main/script_value.c  | 10 ++++++----
 src/main/tournament.c    |  2 +-
 src/main/utils2.c        |  4 ++--
 8 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/dw/model.h b/include/dw/model.h
index c7b0b0b..9e62ac7 100644
